# Web UI

`web/` is a React 18 + TypeScript + Vite SPA styled with Tailwind and `lucide-react`. No router and no extra state library: `App.tsx` holds tab state and loads data through `web/src/api.ts`.

- Add request functions to `api.ts` and shared types to `types.ts`. Components in `web/src/components/` receive data and callbacks; they do not call `fetch` directly.
- Talk to the native API at `/api/v1`. The Vite dev server proxies `/api`, `/sonarr`, `/radarr`, and `/prowlarr` to `:8989`.
- Auth token key is `replacearr_token`. Send `Authorization: Bearer` via the shared `request()` helper.
- Match existing function components, explicit prop types, and Tailwind utility classes.
- After UI changes, run `cd web && npm run typecheck`. Production builds land in `web/dist` and are copied to `internal/webui/dist` by `make build-web`.
- The production app is an installable PWA. Manifest and worker live in `web/public/manifest.webmanifest` and `web/public/sw.js`, and `main.tsx` registers the worker only in production builds. Keep `display: standalone`. The worker must not cache non-GET API calls.

```tsx
// BAD: fetch inside a tab component
const res = await fetch('/api/v1/series');

// GOOD: go through the shared client
const series = await api.listSeries();
```
